  "interpretation": "<ol><li><p>Negative or Non-detectable: If the Rh antibody titre is negative or non-detectable, it indicates the absence or very low level of Rh antibodies in the blood. This is considered a normal or non-reactive result, indicating that the individual does not have significant Rh antibodies.</p></li><li><p>Positive or Detectable: If the Rh antibody titre is positive or detectable, it suggests the presence of Rh antibodies in the blood. The specific level or titre value will indicate the concentration of Rh antibodies present.</p></li></ol>",
